# Backend Rules (`apps/api`)

Stack: NestJS, Better Auth (cookie session via `@elynd/auth` + `@thallesp/nestjs-better-auth`), Drizzle (`@elynd/db`), Zod (`@elynd/shared`), Vitest.

Placement and package boundaries: **`layering.mdc`** + **`decisions.mdc`** (framework-agnostic; follow those first).

Auth executable contracts: [`.trellis/spec/api/backend/auth-monorepo.md`](../../.trellis/spec/api/backend/auth-monorepo.md) when touching auth.

## TypeScript

- Extend `../../tsconfig.base.json`; keep Nest-only flags (`experimentalDecorators`, `emitDecoratorMetadata`, …) in this app's `tsconfig.json`
- Keep `outDir` / `rootDir` / `include` / `types` local
- **Imports (N1):** relative NodeNext imports with `.js` suffixes inside the API. Do **not** enable `@/` path aliases in emitted code until a Nest emit rewrite (e.g. `tsc-alias`) is added
- **Nest DI + `import type`:** constructor-injected classes/tokens must remain **value** imports. Prefer `@Inject(Token)` so `consistent-type-imports` does not erase runtime tokens. Pure type-only imports are fine for interfaces and for params already tagged with `@Inject(…)`

## Layout (Nest mapping of layering)

| Folder | Role |
| ------ | ---- |
| `src/modules/<domain>/` | Feature modules — business workflows. Create this directory when the first domain lands; do **not** pre-create an empty `modules/` folder |
| `src/common/` | Transport cross-cutting: pipes, filters, decorators — **no** domain workflows (flat; no artifact-type subfolders) |
| `src/global/` | Global DI assembly (`global.module.ts`) and colocated global providers |
| `scripts/` | Offline TypeScript tooling (e.g. OpenAPI gen) — not HTTP runtime; run with `pnpm exec tsx` (see `openapi:gen`). Included in `tsconfig.json` for IDE/typecheck; excluded from Nest `tsconfig.build.json` emit |

- Thin controllers: validate + map HTTP; business rules in injectable services
- Auth instance lives in `@elynd/auth/server`; wire via `AuthModule.forRoot` in `AppModule`. Load env before importing auth (`load-env.ts`)
- Prefer `@elynd/auth` inferred types (`AuthUser` / `AuthSession`); do not reinvent session user shapes in apps
- Tech helpers with zero domain knowledge may live under `common/` or small dedicated folders — never import feature modules from tech helpers
- Do not use Adonis-style Access Token auth on the Nest path

## Validation & OpenAPI

- Prefer shared Zod helpers from `@elynd/shared/schemas` (pagination, common shapes)
- Compose feature HTTP DTOs from `@elynd/db` drizzle-zod in the feature module
- Use project Zod validation pipe in `src/common`; generate OpenAPI via `openapi:gen` → `scripts/generate-openapi.ts` with `pnpm exec tsx` (`createOpenApiDocument`) for Apifox — do not mount Swagger UI
- Swagger DTO `@ApiProperty` must set explicit `type` when scripts run under tsx (no `emitDecoratorMetadata`)
- Do not duplicate the same request/response schema in the web app — put cross-app contracts in `@elynd/shared`

## Env

Required auth-related keys: `DATABASE_URI`, `AUTH_SECRET`, `BETTER_AUTH_URL`, `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` (validated by `@elynd/auth/env`).

## Lint

Root `eslint.config.mjs` (run via `pnpm lint` / `pnpm -w exec eslint apps/api`).
